#: ../../docs/about/list_of_features.rst:239
msgid "**Physically-based rendering (built-in material features):**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../docs/about/list_of_features.rst:241
msgid "Follows the Disney PBR model."
msgstr ""

#: ../../docs/about/list_of_features.rst:242
msgid "Supports Burley, Lambert, Lambert Wrap (half-Lambert) and Toon diffuse shading modes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../docs/about/list_of_features.rst:243
msgid "Supports Schlick-GGX, Toon and Disabled specular shading modes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../docs/about/list_of_features.rst:244
msgid "Uses a roughness-metallic workflow with support for ORM textures."
msgstr ""

#: ../../docs/about/list_of_features.rst:245
msgid "Uses horizon specular occlusion (Filament model) to improve material appearance."
msgstr ""

#: ../../docs/about/list_of_features.rst:246
msgid "Normal mapping."
msgstr ""

#: ../../docs/about/list_of_features.rst:247
msgid "Parallax/relief mapping with automatic level of detail based on distance."
msgstr ""

#: ../../docs/about/list_of_features.rst:248
msgid "Detail mapping for the albedo and normal maps."
msgstr ""

#: ../../docs/about/list_of_features.rst:249
msgid "Subsurface scattering and transmittance."
msgstr ""

#: ../../docs/about/list_of_features.rst:250
msgid "Screen-space refraction with support for material roughness (resulting in blurry refraction)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../docs/about/list_of_features.rst:251
msgid "Proximity fade (soft particles) and distance fade."
msgstr ""

#: ../../docs/about/list_of_features.rst:252
msgid "Distance fade can use alpha blending or dithering to avoid going through the transparent pipeline."
msgstr ""

#: ../../docs/about/list_of_features.rst:254
msgid "Dithering can be determined on a per-pixel or per-object basis."
msgstr ""

#: ../../docs/about/list_of_features.rst:256
msgid "**Real-time lighting:**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../docs/about/list_of_features.rst:258
msgid ":ref:`Directional lights <doc_lights_and_shadows_directional_light>` (sun/moon)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../docs/about/list_of_features.rst:259
msgid ":ref:`Omnidirectional lights <doc_lights_and_shadows_omni_light>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../docs/about/list_of_features.rst:260
msgid ":ref:`Spot lights <doc_lights_and_shadows_spot_light>` with adjustable cone angle and attenuation."
msgstr ""

#: ../../docs/about/list_of_features.rst:261
msgid ":ref:`Rectangular area lights <doc_lights_and_shadows_area_light>` with an optional texture to determine the shape and color."
msgstr ""

#: ../../docs/about/list_of_features.rst:263
msgid "Specular, indirect light, and volumetric fog energy can be adjusted on a per-light basis."
msgstr ""

#: ../../docs/about/list_of_features.rst:264
msgid "Adjustable light \"size\" for spherical omni and disc spot lights (will also make shadows blurrier with variable penumbra)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../docs/about/list_of_features.rst:266
msgid "Optional distance fade system to fade distant lights and their shadows, improving performance."
msgstr ""

#: ../../docs/about/list_of_features.rst:267
msgid "When using the Forward+ renderer (default on desktop), lights are rendered with clustered forward optimizations to decrease their individual cost. Clustered rendering also lifts any limits on the number of lights that can be used on a mesh."
msgstr ""

#: ../../docs/about/list_of_features.rst:270
msgid "When using the Mobile renderer, up to 8 omni lights, 8 spot lights, and 8 area lights can be displayed per mesh resource. Baked lighting can be used to overcome this limit if needed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../docs/about/list_of_features.rst:274
msgid "**Shadow mapping:**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../docs/about/list_of_features.rst:276
msgid "*DirectionalLight3D:* Orthogonal (fastest), PSSM 2-split and 4-split. Supports blending between splits."
msgstr ""

#: ../../docs/about/list_of_features.rst:278
msgid "*OmniLight3D:* Dual paraboloid (fast) or cubemap (slower but more accurate). Supports colored projector textures in the form of panoramas."
msgstr ""

#: ../../docs/about/list_of_features.rst:280
msgid "*SpotLight3D:* Single texture. Supports colored projector textures."
msgstr ""

#: ../../docs/about/list_of_features.rst:281
msgid "*AreaLight3D:* Single texture with dual paraboloid distortion to approximate the light's shape."
msgstr ""

#: ../../docs/about/list_of_features.rst:283
msgid "Shadow normal offset bias and shadow pancaking to decrease the amount of visible shadow acne and peter-panning."
msgstr ""

#: ../../docs/about/list_of_features.rst:285
msgid ":abbr:`PCSS (Percentage Closer Soft Shadows)`-like shadow blur based on the light size and distance from the surface the shadow is cast on. Supported for all light types."
msgstr ""

#: ../../docs/about/list_of_features.rst:288
msgid "Adjustable shadow blur on a per-light basis."
msgstr ""

#: ../../docs/about/list_of_features.rst:290
msgid "**Global illumination with indirect lighting:**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../docs/about/list_of_features.rst:292
msgid ":ref:`Baked lightmaps <doc_using_lightmap_gi>` (fast, but can't be updated at runtime)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../docs/about/list_of_features.rst:294
msgid "Supports baking indirect light only or baking both direct and indirect lighting. The bake mode can be adjusted on a per-light basis to allow for hybrid light baking setups."
msgstr ""

#: ../../docs/about/list_of_features.rst:297
msgid "Supports lighting dynamic objects using automatic and manually placed probes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../docs/about/list_of_features.rst:298
msgid "Optionally supports directional lighting based on spherical harmonics."
msgstr ""

#: ../../docs/about/list_of_features.rst:299
msgid "Optionally supports baking a shadowmask for distant static directional shadows."
msgstr ""

#: ../../docs/about/list_of_features.rst:300
msgid "Optional supersampling at bake-time to improve quality and reduce light leaking at the cost of increased bake times and memory usage during baking."
msgstr ""

#: ../../docs/about/list_of_features.rst:302
msgid "Lightmaps are baked on the GPU using compute shaders (much faster than CPU lightmapping). Baking can only be performed from the editor, not in exported projects."
msgstr ""

#: ../../docs/about/list_of_features.rst:305
msgid "Supports GPU-based :ref:`denoising <doc_using_lightmap_gi_denoising>` with JNLM out of the box, or higher-quality CPU/GPU-based denoising with OIDN (requires downloading OIDN separately)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../docs/about/list_of_features.rst:308
msgid "Lightmaps are rendered with bicubic filtering to reduce scaling artifacts."
msgstr ""

#: ../../docs/about/list_of_features.rst:310
msgid ":ref:`Voxel-based GI probes <doc_using_voxel_gi>`. Supports dynamic lights *and* dynamic occluders, while also supporting reflections. Requires a fast baking step which can be performed in the editor or at runtime (including from an exported project)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../docs/about/list_of_features.rst:314
msgid ":ref:`Signed-distance field GI <doc_using_sdfgi>` designed for large open worlds. Supports dynamic lights, but not dynamic occluders. Supports reflections. No baking required."
msgstr ""

#: ../../docs/about/list_of_features.rst:317
msgid ":ref:`Screen-space indirect lighting (SSIL) <doc_environment_and_post_processing_ssil>` at half or full resolution. Fully real-time and supports any kind of emissive light source (including decals)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../docs/about/list_of_features.rst:320
msgid "VoxelGI and SDFGI use a deferred pass to allow for rendering GI at half resolution to improve performance (while still having functional MSAA support)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../docs/about/list_of_features.rst:323
msgid "**Reflections:**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../docs/about/list_of_features.rst:325
msgid "Voxel-based reflections (when using GI probes) and SDF-based reflections (when using signed distance field GI). Voxel-based reflections are visible on transparent surfaces, while rough SDF-based reflections are visible on transparent surfaces."
msgstr ""

#: ../../docs/about/list_of_features.rst:329
msgid "Fast baked reflections or slow real-time reflections using ReflectionProbe. Parallax box correction can optionally be enabled."
msgstr ""

#: ../../docs/about/list_of_features.rst:331
msgid "Screen-space reflections with support for material roughness."
msgstr ""

#: ../../docs/about/list_of_features.rst:332
msgid "Reflection techniques can be mixed together for greater accuracy or scalability."
msgstr ""

#: ../../docs/about/list_of_features.rst:333
msgid "When using the Forward+ renderer (default on desktop), reflection probes are rendered with clustered forward optimizations to decrease their individual cost. Clustered rendering also lifts any limits on the number of reflection probes that can be used on a mesh."
msgstr ""

#: ../../docs/about/list_of_features.rst:337
msgid "When using the Mobile renderer, up to 8 reflection probes can be displayed per mesh resource. When using the Compatibility renderer, up to 2 reflection probes can be displayed per mesh resource."
msgstr ""

#: ../../docs/about/list_of_features.rst:341
msgid "**Decals:**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../docs/about/list_of_features.rst:343
msgid ":ref:`Supports albedo <doc_using_decals>`, emissive, :abbr:`ORM (Occlusion Roughness Metallic)`, and normal mapping."
msgstr ""

#: ../../docs/about/list_of_features.rst:345
msgid "Texture channels are smoothly overlaid on top of the underlying material, with support for normal/ORM-only decals."
msgstr ""

#: ../../docs/about/list_of_features.rst:347
msgid "Support for normal fade to fade the decal depending on its incidence angle."
msgstr ""

#: ../../docs/about/list_of_features.rst:348
msgid "Does not rely on runtime mesh generation. This means decals can be used on complex skinned meshes with no performance penalty, even if the decal moves every frame."
msgstr ""

#: ../../docs/about/list_of_features.rst:350
